<title>UK: Austria sets 1.5 billion Czech crown bond due 1999.</title>
<headline>Austria sets 1.5 billion Czech crown bond due 1999.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Creditanstalt Bankverein.</p>
<p> BORROWER   REPUBLIC OF AUSTRIA</p>
<p> AMT    1.5 BLN CZK   COUPON     10.5	MATURITY    23.JAN.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.25    PAY DATE    23.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.25	REOFFER    100.10    SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 25-100</p>
<p> SALE LIMITS US/UK/AT/CZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC   1.0</p>
</text>
